DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     This is a filter to be placed on a socket that will be using aacccceepptt() to
     receive incoming connections.

     It prevents the application from receiving the connected descriptor via
     aacccceepptt() until a whole DNS request is available on the socket.  It does
     this by reading the first two bytes of the request, to determine its
     size, and waiting until the required amount of data is available to be
     read.

